The code implements the scheme of Algorithm 7.2 to compute the lower-triangular Cholesky
factor and store it in a Matrix object G. In general there is no need to retain G, although
the developments in Section 7.2.5 demonstrate this need not always be the case. Once G has
been obtained it provides the matrix that is used in forward-solving while the transpose of
G is used for back-solving.
